# ── esheet-frontend environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to ".env" (or ".env.production") and adjust before building.
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the app — never put
# secrets here: everything VITE_* ends up readable in the browser bundle.

# Base URL of the e-Sheet backend API, including the /api path.
#
# Development: LEAVE UNSET. The app defaults to the relative path "/api",
# which the Vite dev server proxies to http://localhost:5000 (see
# vite.config.js). Works from desktop AND phones on the LAN over one HTTPS
# origin — no hardcoded IPs.
#
# Production (API on a separate domain):
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.com/api
# Production behind the same reverse proxy as the frontend: leave unset and
# route /api on the proxy instead.
# VITE_API_URL=
